WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy- and Golden Globe-winning

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
actor you know from his work
in "The Big Lebowski,"

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Artist,"
and "The Righteous Gemstones."

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:09.776
He stars in "The Conners," which
returns January 13th on ABC.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.777 line:92%
Please welcome back to the sho

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
our very good friend
John Goodman.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
John, how are you?

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Swell! How you doing, Seth?
Happy new year.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Happy new year to you.
I feel like this is the closes

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.653 line:92%
our haircuts have ever been.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pretty much.
I got a COVID-19 cut.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:24.924 line:92%
-Yeah, same here. Same here.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know were you in New Orleans
for a long time.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're back in L.A.
shooting "The Conners" now

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was your time
in New Orleans?

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.966 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It was great.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Chuckles ]
I didn't want to leave.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
The streets were a little
emptier than usual,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.672 line:92%
but it was good to be home

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.509 size:78% position:39%
-You know, obviously,
New Orleans known for

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.610 size:78% position:39% line:92%
its live music scene.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
Live music clubs are getting
hit hard, very hard.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.816 size:75% position:38%
You did a fundraiser
on New Year's Eve.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you feel about thos
live music venues?

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:55.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
And do you have some favorites
in New Orleans?

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.390 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, I do, but it's...

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, they're really
getting whacked,

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's been that way
for a long time.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:07.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
I met my wife at Tipitina'
in like 1988.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:10.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she kind of thought
I was a zombie,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I had a buddy of mine
keep track of her,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we started dating
a year later.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I kind of stalked her,
real long-distance.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.349
-[ Laughs ] But it's worked out,
obviously.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So far! 31 years.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys are back
doing "The Conners."

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.689 line:92%
It's a show that's filmed

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of a live
studio audience.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't have one,
I'm assuming.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not anymore.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
We get a lot more done.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:42.001 line:92%
No, we shoot it differently now.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those guys will laugh
at anything,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's kind of hard
to time things sometimes.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember going to a sho
in the studio audience.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you really are sort of
whipped into a frenzy

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.614 size:78% position:39%
by the warm-up comic,
which is their job

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they do
a very good job at it,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:59.986
but I can imagine sometime
it messes with comic rhythm.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, they're in this frenz
for hours, you see.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:07.727
And I guess they like to hea
themselves on the playback

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.895 line:92%
when they watch it at home

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, it's impossible
to time anything.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it hard to generate
the same performance level

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.972
without an audience, or ar
you guys finding it's okay

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's okay, but we really
got to think about it

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.844
and remember that that's
a whole nother energy leve

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you got people
in the audience.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Laughing at everything.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We, of course,
first met at "SNL,"

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.317 line:92%
which is a live studio audienc

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is not whipped
into a frenzy

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the same way
that a sitcom audience is.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember
Norm Macdonald once said

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:41.094
he thought it was the last
true audience in television,

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:44.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they're just --
you can just bomb on "SNL"

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.566 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like nowhere else.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.369 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, and it's weird
when you watch it --

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:52.038
when you're doing the show
and you watch it played back

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:55.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the studio audienc
is a lot louder

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.111 line:92%
than they amplify it at home

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.379 line:92%
So you could be doing alright,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it sounds like you jus
murdered somebody.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Conners" is actually gonn
address the pandemic,

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.354 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which is no surprise.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a show that has
addressed real-life issues

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
very modern issues,

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
things up to and including
even opioid addition --

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.830 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Addiction. Excuse me.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it interesting
to be doing a show

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.835
that's sort of addressing issues
in real time?

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:26.105
-Yeah, sure, 'cause everybod
brings their two cents into it

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.408 line:92%
things they've experienced

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, why pretend
it's not there?

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.746 line:92%
I personally would rather

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
have them let me solve crime
on the show.

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.817 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] You should.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:41.554 size:75% position:38%
Have you ever solved
a crime on a show?

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'd like to.
I'd like to start doing that

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at home, as well.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:49.329
-Well, I feel like if you solved
a couple crimes

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.897 size:75% position:38% line:92%
on your own at home,

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:54.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
then they'd spin it
into a TV show immediately

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If I talk to some guys
about it first.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.005 line:92%
You know, kick the interest up

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were one of my favorite
shows from --

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.109 line:92%
I guess now two years ago.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.611 line:92%
That's how time is moving.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.845 line:92%
"The Righteous Gemstones."

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you guys were going bac
to do a second season

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
that got sort of waylaid b
everything we're going through

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.752 line:92%
That must be a fun show to do.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:16.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's great.
Just every day is a lot of fun

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:20.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
Working with some
spectacular people,

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.661 line:92%
and the situations are great

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:25.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's gonna be a doozy this yea
from what I'm reading.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:26.899 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But, yeah, we got there,

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got my clothes
out of the suitcase

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:32.739
and groceries in for the -
getting ready to start work,

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:35.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they canned us
for two months,

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.577 line:92%
which turned into permanently.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.479 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I love Danny McBride,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:42.081
but Walton Goggins has bee
one of my long favorites.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.517 size:88% position:44%
And I will say, the feud
between the two of you

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.387 line:92%
is just a delight to watch

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.621 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah. He's terrific.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.190 line:92%
He's just incredibly funny

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.794
-Exciting news was announced
that you and Billy Crystal

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.195 line:92%
are going to be the voices

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:59.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a "Monsters Inc."
television show.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.600 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That was a show that --

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
that movie, I should say,
came out so long ago.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it exciting
to come back to it?

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:07.907 line:92%
-Yeah. It's a lot of fun.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't -- I haven't gotte
to work with Billy

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.578 size:84% position:42% line:92%
in the same studio yet.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.548 line:92%
That really gooses the energy,

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's
hard to keep up with.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.086 line:92%
-Your daughter was very youn

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:22.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the first "Monsters Inc."
came out.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
As she grew up, what of your
work has she engaged with

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:29.329 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and enjoyed the most?

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ah, not really
any of them, so...

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No? Not a Lebowski fan?
-Nah.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just,
"Dad's home again. Eh."

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:45.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, a lot of kids,
that's what they know me from.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:45.912 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That voice.

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And when they hear it,
do they...

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you tell when
a kid hears your voice

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:51.451 line:92%
and recognizes it from that?

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know they recognize
something.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Something's wrong
with this guy."

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.990 size:84% position:42%
-I mean, there could be
any number of reasons

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.060
they react that there's
something wrong with you.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You realize that?

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:03.296 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It might not just be

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:06.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they recognize your voice
from "Monsters Inc."

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:08.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the same vibe.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.870 line:92%
There's just gradations of it.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:11.804 line:92%
You have to be aware of that

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.307
-I'm gonna let you go 'cause
I know you have some crime

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:16.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
to solve in the house.
-Thanks, Seth.

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-John, it's always a delight
to see you.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.279 line:92%
Thanks so much for being here.

